# Project Rules

## Documentation must be kept in sync
Whenever you add, change, or remove a user-facing feature, command, or behaviour in this
project, you MUST also update the relevant documentation before considering the task complete:

- `docs/USER_GUIDE.md` — the end-user guide (toolbar menu, map features, behaviours, legends).
- `README.md` — the developer/feature overview, including the Android-vs-iOS feature-comparison
  table and the signal-propagation notes.

This applies to new menu items, exported formats, map overlays/labels, settings, and any
behaviour change a user would notice. Do not leave docs stale after a code change.

## Only push to the repo after a version change
Do NOT push commits to the remote repository unless the app version has been bumped in the
same change. Codemagic builds on every push, so pushing without a version bump wastes build
minutes/money for no release benefit.

- The iOS version lives in `pubspec.yaml` (`version:` — `x.y.z+build`).
- The Android version lives in `app/build.gradle` (`appVersionCode` / `versionName`).
- Bump the relevant version (and build number) as part of the change that you are pushing.
- Pure doc-only or non-release commits should be kept local (or squashed into the next
  version-bump commit) rather than pushed on their own.
